# Agent boundaries

## Ask before editing
- `compose.env`, `**/appsettings.*.local.json`, user-secrets, Key Vault refs
- `Directory.Build.props`, `*.sln`, `*.csproj`, `docker-compose.yml`
- `features.json` — only structural renames/removals; routine slice entries from `/new-slice` or `/new-module` are OK
- EF migrations (create/remove) — confirm intent + name

## Never auto-run
- `git push --force`, hard reset, mass delete
- `rm -rf` on a path that differs from an existing one only by case. macOS resolves `src/App` and
  `src/app` to the **same** directory, so a backend path typed from inside `src/web/` deletes the
  front end. Use absolute paths and `ls` the target first.
- Commits / PRs unless the user explicitly asked
- Prod/staging mutators (deploy, DB drop, secret rotate)

## Secrets
- Do not commit real passwords, connection strings, or API keys
- Dev seed creds in docs are Development-only; never reuse in prod config
- If a secret appears in chat/diff/logs: stop, tell the user to rotate, do not repeat the value

## Dependencies
- Prefer packages already in the solution; justify any new NuGet package before adding

## Work quality
- No symptom-only workarounds without a root-cause note in the reply
- Before concluding multi-step work: check `git status` / diff and run `make verify` (or the smallest relevant test filter)
